{Double attack is one of the most important motif in chess. Double attack is
called when we attack two pieces of the opponent in one move!} 1. e6 {The pawn
moves forward and attacks both knights, creating a double attack, White wins
material. This kind of double attack is also called as "fork" as the pawn
creates a fork by threatening to take to both directions.} Nd6 2. exd7 $18 *

[Event "?"]
[Site "?"]
[Date "????.??.??"]
[Round "?"]
[White "Double attack"]
[Black "sample 2"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/6kp/1pBbnpp1/p1p5/4K3/1P3NP1/P1P2P1P/8 w - - 0 1"]
[PlyCount "3"]
[SourceDate "2018.03.29"]

{Double attacks can be executed with all the pieces. Sometimes it is even
possible with the king. For example in this position with plays} 1. Kd5 {
double attacks the knight and the bishop and one of the pieces gets lost.} Kf7
2. Kxd6 $18 {In this chapter, you will need to find a lot of hidden double
attack to win material.} *

